; Build-time: create the dedicated FAST namespace (HS-enabled, interoperability
; on) and stand up the real FHIR R4 endpoint at /fhir-agent-studio/fhir/r4.
; Runs BEFORE the IPM module load (iris.script) so FAST exists for zpm.
;
; HS.Util.Installer.Foundation.Install creates the database + namespace, maps the
; HS libraries, enables Ensemble/interoperability, and auto-runs the FHIR
; InstallNamespace base setup. InstallInstance then registers our specific R4
; endpoint backed by the JSON interactions strategy.
do ##class(HS.Util.Installer.Foundation).Install("FAST")
zn "FAST"
do ##class(HS.FHIRServer.Installer).InstallInstance("/fhir-agent-studio/fhir/r4", "HS.FHIRServer.Storage.Json.InteractionsStrategy", "hl7.fhir.r4.core@4.0.1")
; Verify the endpoint registered; abort the build (non-zero) if not, so a broken
; image is never produced silently.
if '##class(%SYS.Namespace).Exists("FAST") do $system.Process.Terminate($job, 1)
write !,"FAST-NAMESPACE-READY",!
halt
